# API and backend integration

## HTTP client

- One shared Axios instance (e.g. `services/http.ts`).
- `baseURL` from env (`import.meta.env.VITE_API_BASE_URL`). Never hardcode API hosts or paths in components.
- Attach `Authorization: Bearer <token>` in a request interceptor when a token exists.
- Handle 401 (and consistent envelope failures) in a response interceptor — clear session and route to login as decided in auth rules.
- Surface network/server errors; do not swallow them silently.

## Envelope

Backend returns:

```ts
interface ApiResponse<T> {
  success: boolean
  message: string
  data: T | null
  pagination: null
  errors: Record<string, string[]> | null
}

interface PagedApiResponse<T> {
  success: boolean
  message: string
  data: T | null
  pagination: PaginationMetadata
  errors: Record<string, string[]> | null
}
```

- Non-paged endpoints: `pagination` is always `null`.
- Paged lists: read `pagination` (`pageNumber`, `pageSize`, `totalCount`, `totalPages`, `hasPreviousPage`, `hasNextPage`).
- Check `success` and map `message` / `errors` for UI feedback. Do not assume `data` is present on failure.

## Services

- One service module per API area (`authService`, `userService`, `roleService`, …).
- Views/components call services or stores that call services — never duplicate the same endpoint call in multiple SFCs.
- Query params for lists: `pageNumber`, `pageSize` (backend defaults 1 / 20, max 100).
